[{:db/id 17592186092338 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-29b59535-24cf-5f4f-a890-c8446f20f105" "question-1bca56bb-980a-59df-8356-0638316b5266"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186091945 :question/problem "$$\n\\mathbf{1}_{A}(-1) = 0, \\qquad \\mathbf{1}_{B}(-1) = 1\n$$\n\nGiven the values of the indicator functions of the sets $A$ and $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\mathbf{1}_{A \\,\\cup\\, B}\\,(-1) = 1$\n\nII. $\\mathbf{1}_{A \\,\\cup\\, B}\\,(-1) = 0$\n\nIII. $-1 \\in A \\cup B$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-29b59535-24cf-5f4f-a890-c8446f20f105" :question/id #uuid "29b59535-24cf-5f4f-a890-c8446f20f105" :question/math-academy-id "q-174368" :question/problem "Which of the following is the indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ of the subset $A={2,4,8}$ of $X={0,2,4,6,8}.$" :question/worked-solution "An indicator function maps elements from a set to the values $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether the element belongs to a specified subset. The indicator function is designed to \"indicate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)={\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe indicator function of the set ${2,4,8}$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/85/850019897d92b0a8d3340c091cee15342be20e99e7578a9fca23f88804e3bf28.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the elements $2,4$ and $8$ (the elements of our subset) are mapped to $1,$ and all other elements are mapped to $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cf8ea8f5-c032-5e49-884a-cc5191da30a2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cf8ea8f5-c032-5e49-884a-cc5191da30a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf8ea8f5-c032-5e49-884a-cc5191da30a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correc